Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.36,0:00:22.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,今天的《造物小百科》：
Dialogue: 1,0:00:21.36,0:00:22.72,Original,,0,0,0,,Today on How It's Made:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.12,0:00:28.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,牙签，工业规模的木雕工艺
Dialogue: 1,0:00:25.12,0:00:28.64,Original,,0,0,0,,Toothpicks, wood carving on an industrial scale,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.08,0:00:34.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,亚克力浴缸，从模具到喷漆的全程揭秘
Dialogue: 1,0:00:30.08,0:00:34.40,Original,,0,0,0,,acrylic bathtubs from mold to spray and beyond,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.40,0:00:39.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,直升机，深入探访一架直升机的诞生
Dialogue: 1,0:00:36.40,0:00:39.44,Original,,0,0,0,,helicopters, a detailed look at the birth of a chopper.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.08,0:00:45.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,还有啤酒，我们喝得够多了，来看看它是怎么做的
Dialogue: 1,0:00:42.08,0:00:45.68,Original,,0,0,0,,And beer, we drink enough of it, so here's how they make it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.88,0:00:47.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,但首先
Dialogue: 1,0:00:46.88,0:00:47.44,Original,,0,0,0,,But first,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.52,0:00:52.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,有人用它们串起餐前小点
Dialogue: 1,0:00:49.52,0:00:52.00,Original,,0,0,0,,some people use them to hold together hors d'oeuvres,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.32,0:00:56.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,也有人用它们搭建著名建筑和桥梁的模型
Dialogue: 1,0:00:52.32,0:00:56.00,Original,,0,0,0,,while others make scale models of famous buildings and bridges out of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.80,0:00:59.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,还有人用它们来履行本分职责
Dialogue: 1,0:00:56.80,0:00:59.36,Original,,0,0,0,,Some even use them for their primary purpose,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.68,0:01:01.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,清除卡在牙缝里的食物残渣
Dialogue: 1,0:00:59.68,0:01:01.76,Original,,0,0,0,,to remove food caught between their teeth.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.96,0:01:06.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,欢迎来到生产小小牙签的工厂
Dialogue: 1,0:01:02.96,0:01:06.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Welcome to the factory that makes the humble toothpick.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.54,0:01:14.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,制造牙签的原料很简单：
Dialogue: 1,0:01:11.54,0:01:14.32,Original,,0,0,0,,The raw materials for making toothpicks is simple:
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.12,0:01:18.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,原木，大量的原木，准确说是桦木
Dialogue: 1,0:01:15.12,0:01:18.88,Original,,0,0,0,,logs, and lots of them, birch logs to be exact.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.90,0:01:26.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,进入剥皮机后，它们的蜕变便开始了
Dialogue: 1,0:01:22.90,0:01:26.40,Original,,0,0,0,,And so begins their transformation as they enter the debarker.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.04,0:01:30.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,树皮虽不能用来做牙签，却也大有用处
Dialogue: 1,0:01:27.04,0:01:30.40,Original,,0,0,0,,Although the bark can't be used for the toothpicks, it does play a role.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.12,0:01:33.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,它被卖给邻近的工厂作燃料
Dialogue: 1,0:01:31.12,0:01:33.92,Original,,0,0,0,,It's sold to a neighbouring factory where it's used as fuel.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.48,0:01:44.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,剥皮机分两步作业
Dialogue: 1,0:01:42.48,0:01:44.80,Original,,0,0,0,,The debarker works in two steps.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.52,0:01:50.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,两次处理后，得到完美圆柱形的木卷，更便于加工
Dialogue: 1,0:01:45.52,0:01:50.56,Original,,0,0,0,,With two passes, it produces a log roll that's perfectly cylindrical and easier to mill.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.78,0:02:05.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台名副其实的"展开机"像撕卷纸一样剥离原木
Dialogue: 1,0:02:01.78,0:02:05.36,Original,,0,0,0,,The aptly named unraveling machine strips the log as if it
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.36,0:02:09.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,用12把细刃将其削成薄片
Dialogue: 1,0:02:05.36,0:02:09.04,Original,,0,0,0,,were a roll of paper, slicing it with 12 fine blades.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.32,0:02:15.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,只有锋利如剃刀的器具才能如此轻松地分解树木
Dialogue: 1,0:02:12.32,0:02:15.68,Original,,0,0,0,,Only razor sharp implements can reduce a tree so easily.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.64,0:02:19.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,同样的刀片稍后还会用来切割牙签
Dialogue: 1,0:02:16.64,0:02:19.68,Original,,0,0,0,,These same blades will be used later to cut toothpicks.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.08,0:02:36.70,Translation,,0,0,0,,下一道工序中，原木很快变身成坯料
Dialogue: 1,0:02:32.08,0:02:36.70,Original,,0,0,0,,The logs are quickly transformed in the next stage of the process: the billets.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.80,0:02:55.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,边切割边卷绕，就形成了坯料
Dialogue: 1,0:02:52.80,0:02:55.92,Original,,0,0,0,,As they're cut, they're rolled, forming the billet itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.76,0:03:08.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,完成后成卷的胚料，被送往冲压机
Dialogue: 1,0:03:03.76,0:03:08.40,Original,,0,0,0,,Completed strips, each a cylinder of coiled trunk, are taken to the puncher.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.24,0:03:17.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,在张力绷紧与滚筒引导下，扁形牙签冲压机把坯条切成大小一致的碎段
Dialogue: 1,0:03:10.24,0:03:17.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Held taut and roller guided, the flat toothpick puncher cuts the billet strips into small, equal-sized pieces.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.96,0:03:31.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,并让它们源源不断地送出
Dialogue: 1,0:03:28.96,0:03:31.20,Original,,0,0,0,,And discharges them in a steady flow.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.76,0:03:42.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,刀片以惊人速度每分钟落下2000次
Dialogue: 1,0:03:37.76,0:03:42.36,Original,,0,0,0,,At an intense speed, the knives come down 2,000 times per minute
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.36,0:03:46.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,短短60秒内总计切割出8000根牙签
Dialogue: 1,0:03:42.36,0:03:46.56,Original,,0,0,0,,to cut a total of 8,000 toothpicks in just 60 seconds.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.36,0:03:53.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,切好的牙签顺着滑槽飞速送进储料槽
Dialogue: 1,0:03:49.36,0:03:53.52,Original,,0,0,0,,Cut toothpicks are spirited away by a chute that leads to a holding tank.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.40,0:03:56.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,此时木材仍然柔软
Dialogue: 1,0:03:54.40,0:03:56.40,Original,,0,0,0,,At this stage, the wood is still soft,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.88,0:04:03.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,所以要在巨型烘干机中120℃处理4小时使其硬化
Dialogue: 1,0:03:56.88,0:04:03.12,Original,,0,0,0,,so needs to be hardened in monster dryers for four hours at 120 degrees centigrade.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.32,0:04:06.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,接着牙签被送往抛光机
Dialogue: 1,0:04:04.32,0:04:06.72,Original,,0,0,0,,Then the toothpicks are transferred to the polisher.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.44,0:04:11.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,4小时里，滑石粉与摩擦共舞
Dialogue: 1,0:04:07.44,0:04:11.84,Original,,0,0,0,,For four hours, a simple dance between talcum powder and friction
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.40,0:04:15.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,打磨出光洁完美的牙签
Dialogue: 1,0:04:12.40,0:04:15.20,Original,,0,0,0,,creates a perfectly smooth toothpick.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.20,0:04:20.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,牙签离开抛光机后经过筛分机，滤除破损的次品
Dialogue: 1,0:04:15.20,0:04:20.00,Original,,0,0,0,,They exit the polisher and pass through a sifter, which filters out broken picks.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.52,0:04:24.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,完好的牙签继续进入鼓风机
Dialogue: 1,0:04:21.52,0:04:24.24,Original,,0,0,0,,Those in good condition continue to an air blower,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.56,0:04:26.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,在此吹除受损的牙签
Dialogue: 1,0:04:24.56,0:04:26.72,Original,,0,0,0,,where any damaged pieces are ejected.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.48,0:04:31.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,完美的牙签被气流吹送到传送带上
Dialogue: 1,0:04:28.48,0:04:31.44,Original,,0,0,0,,The perfect toothpicks are air blown onto a conveyor.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.08,0:04:34.58,Translation,,0,0,0,,末端的滚筒确保按量分配
Dialogue: 1,0:04:32.08,0:04:34.58,Original,,0,0,0,,Drums at the end assure quantity distribution
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.58,0:04:37.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后被送往自动包装机
Dialogue: 1,0:04:34.58,0:04:37.20,Original,,0,0,0,,before they're carried towards the automatic packagers.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.32,0:04:44.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,机器把牙签排列到位
Dialogue: 1,0:04:42.32,0:04:44.56,Original,,0,0,0,,Machines jockey the sticks into position,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.52,0:04:49.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,再折好待装的纸盒
Dialogue: 1,0:04:47.52,0:04:49.76,Original,,0,0,0,,then fold boxes ready for filling.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.64,0:04:54.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,包装机校准为每盒装650根牙签
Dialogue: 1,0:04:50.64,0:04:54.48,Original,,0,0,0,,The packagers are calibrated to place 650 toothpicks
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.56,0:05:00.10,Translation,,0,0,0,,每小时装出惊人的1150盒
Dialogue: 1,0:04:54.56,0:05:00.10,Original,,0,0,0,,per container and fill a staggering 1,150 boxes an hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.76,0:05:09.06,Translation,,0,0,0,,总之，每小时要处理74.75万根牙签
Dialogue: 1,0:05:01.76,0:05:09.06,Original,,0,0,0,,All in all, it handles 747,500 toothpicks every hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.72,0:05:17.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,另一条生产线上，牙签被单独包装
Dialogue: 1,0:05:13.72,0:05:17.92,Original,,0,0,0,,In a separate operation, toothpicks are individually wrapped for distribution
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.00,0:05:19.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,供应给餐馆和航空公司
Dialogue: 1,0:05:18.00,0:05:19.12,Original,,0,0,0,,to restaurants and airlines.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.84,0:05:23.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,这台机器每分钟封装1200根牙签
Dialogue: 1,0:05:19.84,0:05:23.52,Original,,0,0,0,,This machine seals 1,200 toothpicks per minute,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.16,0:05:27.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,自动完成包纸、上胶和裁切
Dialogue: 1,0:05:24.16,0:05:27.36,Original,,0,0,0,,automatically wrapping, gluing, and cutting the paper.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.48,0:05:31.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,这家工厂每天能生产
Dialogue: 1,0:05:28.48,0:05:31.28,Original,,0,0,0,,This factory can manufacture the astronomical number
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.76,0:05:36.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,多达2021.76万根牙签
Dialogue: 1,0:05:31.76,0:05:36.72,Original,,0,0,0,,of 20,217,600 toothpicks every day.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.28,0:05:46.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,从历史来看，人类并不算爱干净
Dialogue: 1,0:05:43.28,0:05:46.64,Original,,0,0,0,,Historically speaking, humans are not the cleanest.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.20,0:05:49.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,每天洗澡是相对新近的习惯
Dialogue: 1,0:05:47.20,0:05:49.68,Original,,0,0,0,,Bathing daily is a relatively new phenomenon.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.24,0:05:52.62,Translation,,0,0,0,,过去人们只在必要时才洗澡
Dialogue: 1,0:05:50.24,0:05:52.62,Original,,0,0,0,,People used to take baths only when necessary
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.62,0:05:55.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,或是生日那天，以先到者为准
Dialogue: 1,0:05:52.62,0:05:55.20,Original,,0,0,0,,or on their birthday, whichever came first.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.32,0:06:01.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,在浴缸里消磨一个下午，是少数幸运儿的日常奢侈
Dialogue: 1,0:05:56.32,0:06:01.04,Original,,0,0,0,,Whiling away the afternoon in a tub is for the lucky few, an everyday luxury.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.08,0:06:07.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,现代浴缸是21世纪复合材料与古老需求的结合
Dialogue: 1,0:06:02.08,0:06:07.68,Original,,0,0,0,,Modern bathtubs are a marriage between 21st century composites and age-old needs.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.80,0:06:13.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,设计师借助设计软件探索新造型，追求极致舒适
Dialogue: 1,0:06:08.80,0:06:13.92,Original,,0,0,0,,The designer explores new shapes via design software to achieve supreme comfort.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.56,0:06:16.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,虚拟设计完成后，就制作出实体模型
Dialogue: 1,0:06:14.56,0:06:16.80,Original,,0,0,0,,From the virtual, a model is produced.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.52,0:06:20.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,这个按1/6比例制作的模型，材质是纸板
Dialogue: 1,0:06:17.52,0:06:20.48,Original,,0,0,0,,This one, made on 1/6 scale, is cardboard.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.96,0:06:22.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,其他模型则是黏土或泡沫塑料制成
Dialogue: 1,0:06:20.96,0:06:22.96,Original,,0,0,0,,But other models are clay or polystyrene.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.16,0:06:28.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,于是，制造浴缸的流程开始了
Dialogue: 1,0:06:26.16,0:06:28.72,Original,,0,0,0,,And so the process of making the bathtub begins.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.92,0:06:34.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,亚克力板材用陶瓷发热元件加热到200℃
Dialogue: 1,0:06:29.92,0:06:34.16,Original,,0,0,0,,An acrylic sheet is heated to 200 degrees centigrade with ceramic elements.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.72,0:06:36.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,直到它变得柔软可塑
Dialogue: 1,0:06:34.72,0:06:36.24,Original,,0,0,0,,When it becomes soft and malleable.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.54,0:06:47.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,模具上成千上万的小孔协同工作，用真空吸住板材
Dialogue: 1,0:06:42.54,0:06:47.28,Original,,0,0,0,,In perfect harmony, thousands of tiny holes in the mould suction the sheet
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.36,0:06:49.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,塑造出完美的形状
Dialogue: 1,0:06:47.36,0:06:49.68,Original,,0,0,0,,by vacuum, creating the perfect shape.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.00,0:06:56.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,颇有些异想天开的装置中，风机为模具降温
Dialogue: 1,0:06:52.00,0:06:56.00,Original,,0,0,0,,In Heath Robinson style, the mould is cooled as ventilators lower its
Dialogue: 2,0:06:52.00,0:06:56.00,Annotation,,0,0,0,,希思·罗宾逊：英式漫画式复杂装置
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.08,0:06:59.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,短短4分钟内将温度降至77℃
Dialogue: 1,0:06:56.08,0:06:59.84,Original,,0,0,0,,temperature to 77 degrees in just four minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.52,0:07:15.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,风机随后移开
Dialogue: 1,0:07:13.52,0:07:15.04,Original,,0,0,0,,The ventilators make way.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.76,0:07:19.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,仅重16公斤，轻松即可取出
Dialogue: 1,0:07:15.76,0:07:19.28,Original,,0,0,0,,Weighing a mere 16 kilos, the mould is easily removed.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.36,0:07:36.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,用另一块亚克力板材，另一台机器制作出同样完美的模具
Dialogue: 1,0:07:31.36,0:07:36.24,Original,,0,0,0,,With another acrylic sheet, a separate machine creates its own perfectly formed mould.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.84,0:07:50.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,新浴缸看似结实，却承受不住水或沐浴者的重量
Dialogue: 1,0:07:45.84,0:07:50.40,Original,,0,0,0,,The new mould may look solid, but it couldn't take the weight of water or bather,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.88,0:07:52.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,所以要用玻璃纤维加固
Dialogue: 1,0:07:50.88,0:07:52.72,Original,,0,0,0,,so it's reinforced with fiberglass.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.36,0:08:03.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,在不断旋转中，玻璃纤维丝与树脂混合
Dialogue: 1,0:07:59.36,0:08:03.20,Original,,0,0,0,,In a never-ending twirl, the fiberglass strands are mixed with resin,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.68,0:08:06.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,再由机械臂吹附到模具上
Dialogue: 1,0:08:03.68,0:08:06.48,Original,,0,0,0,,and then blown onto the mould by a robotic arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.44,0:08:09.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,玻璃纤维与树脂发生化学反应
Dialogue: 1,0:08:07.44,0:08:09.84,Original,,0,0,0,,A chemical reaction between the fiberglass and the
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.92,0:08:12.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,形成坚固的外壳
Dialogue: 1,0:08:09.92,0:08:12.48,Original,,0,0,0,,resin produces a reinforced shell.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.56,0:08:54.02,Translation,,0,0,0,,表面黏稠的模具被送往毛刷和滚轮工位
Dialogue: 1,0:08:50.56,0:08:54.02,Original,,0,0,0,,The viscous mould is transported to the brush and roller area
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.02,0:08:56.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,消除会削弱浴缸的气泡
Dialogue: 1,0:08:54.02,0:08:56.88,Original,,0,0,0,,where bubbles that weaken the tub are eliminated.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.68,0:09:01.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,75分钟后，层压工艺让玻璃纤维树脂
Dialogue: 1,0:08:57.68,0:09:01.84,Original,,0,0,0,,After 75 minutes, this laminating process makes the fiberglass resin
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.84,0:09:04.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,与亚克力外壳完美贴合
Dialogue: 1,0:09:01.84,0:09:04.08,Original,,0,0,0,,adhere perfectly to the acrylic shell.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.72,0:09:12.78,Translation,,0,0,0,,现已完全干硬的壳体被送到铣削车间
Dialogue: 1,0:09:08.72,0:09:12.78,Original,,0,0,0,,The shell now perfectly dry and hard is taken to the milling department
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.78,0:09:16.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,数控机床开始修整浴缸的边缘
Dialogue: 1,0:09:12.78,0:09:16.88,Original,,0,0,0,,where digitally controlled machines begin trimming the edges of the bathtub.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.08,0:09:27.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,在这道工序中，机器人会开凿排水口、
Dialogue: 1,0:09:24.08,0:09:27.84,Original,,0,0,0,,During this operation, the robot will cut openings for the drains,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.00,0:09:30.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,按摩喷头和气泡喷口、溢水孔
Dialogue: 1,0:09:28.00,0:09:30.88,Original,,0,0,0,,the whirlpool and air jets, the overflow hole,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.88,0:09:33.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,甚至还有水下灯座
Dialogue: 1,0:09:30.88,0:09:33.44,Original,,0,0,0,,and even the underwater light sockets.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.76,0:09:50.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,另一个车间正等待着近乎完工的浴缸
Dialogue: 1,0:09:47.76,0:09:50.88,Original,,0,0,0,,Another workshop awaits the almost completed bathtub.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.36,0:09:56.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,安装水泵以及鼓风机的管路
Dialogue: 1,0:09:53.36,0:09:56.48,Original,,0,0,0,,A pump is installed, along with the piping for the air blower.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.88,0:10:03.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,接着安装按摩系统的水泵
Dialogue: 1,0:10:00.88,0:10:03.60,Original,,0,0,0,,The whirlpool system then has its pump installed,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.60,0:10:08.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,还有PVC管道，接头都已密封以防渗漏
Dialogue: 1,0:10:03.60,0:10:08.96,Original,,0,0,0,,as well as the PVC pipes, whose joints have been hermetically sealed to prevent any leaks.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.16,0:10:18.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,最后，为确保一切运转正常
Dialogue: 1,0:10:16.16,0:10:18.80,Original,,0,0,0,,Finally, to make sure that everything is functioning well,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.20,0:10:21.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,每只浴缸都要通过注水测试
Dialogue: 1,0:10:19.20,0:10:21.52,Original,,0,0,0,,each bathtub undergoes a water test.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.60,0:10:27.94,Translation,,0,0,0,,历经13道工序、5个小时的打造
Dialogue: 1,0:10:23.60,0:10:27.94,Original,,0,0,0,,Through 13 steps of manufacturing and 5 hours of work
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.94,0:10:30.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,浴缸已恭候您入浴
Dialogue: 1,0:10:27.94,0:10:30.96,Original,,0,0,0,, the bathtub is ready to invite you in.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.28,0:10:36.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,本期《造物小百科》稍后播出：直升机
Dialogue: 1,0:10:33.28,0:10:36.24,Original,,0,0,0,,Coming up on how it's made: helicopters.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.88,0:10:39.10,Translation,,0,0,0,,深入探访一架直升机的诞生
Dialogue: 1,0:10:36.88,0:10:39.10,Original,,0,0,0,,A detailed look at the birth of a chopper
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.10,0:10:44.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,3419个零件被组装成一架传说中的飞行器
Dialogue: 1,0:10:39.10,0:10:44.72,Original,,0,0,0,,As 3,419 parts are assembled to create the fabled flying machine.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.42,0:10:47.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,还有啤酒
Dialogue: 1,0:10:46.42,0:10:47.20,Original,,0,0,0,,And beer.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.08,0:10:52.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,它和文明一样古老，足有6000年历史
Dialogue: 1,0:10:48.08,0:10:52.96,Original,,0,0,0,,It's been around for as long as civilization has, a good 6,000 years.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.44,0:10:54.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,广告之后请继续收看
Dialogue: 1,0:10:53.44,0:10:54.72,Original,,0,0,0,,Join us after the break.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.48,0:11:06.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,欢迎回到《造物小百科》
Dialogue: 1,0:11:04.48,0:11:06.24,Original,,0,0,0,,Welcome back to how it's made.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.52,0:11:08.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,稍后我们来看啤酒
Dialogue: 1,0:11:07.52,0:11:08.64,Original,,0,0,0,,Later we look at beer.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.68,0:11:13.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,它和文明一样古老，足有6000年历史
Dialogue: 1,0:11:09.68,0:11:13.76,Original,,0,0,0,,It's been around for as long as civilization has, a good 6,000 years.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.36,0:11:19.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,但首先，列奥纳多·达·芬奇或许画出了最早的设计草图
Dialogue: 1,0:11:15.36,0:11:19.76,Original,,0,0,0,,But first, Leonardo da Vinci may have sketched the first ever designs.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.00,0:11:22.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,但自此以后，这只"天空之鸟"已今非昔比
Dialogue: 1,0:11:20.00,0:11:22.80,Original,,0,0,0,,But this bird of the skies has come a long way since.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.52,0:11:27.10,Translation,,0,0,0,,直升机在像越南战争这样的冲突中崭露头角
Dialogue: 1,0:11:23.52,0:11:27.10,Original,,0,0,0,,The helicopter came into its own during conflicts like Vietnam
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.10,0:11:29.78,Translation,,0,0,0,,丛林作战意味着没有跑道
Dialogue: 1,0:11:27.10,0:11:29.78,Original,,0,0,0,,where jungle warfare meant no runways
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.78,0:11:32.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,需要空运并补给部队
Dialogue: 1,0:11:29.78,0:11:32.24,Original,,0,0,0,,And a need to airlift and resupply troops.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.80,0:11:35.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,那么就随我们一起，见证一架直升机的诞生
Dialogue: 1,0:11:32.80,0:11:35.92,Original,,0,0,0,,So join us as we take a look at the birth of a chopper.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.22,0:11:41.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,直升机多才多艺，让飞行员能够
Dialogue: 1,0:11:38.22,0:11:41.44,Original,,0,0,0,,The versatility of the helicopter allows aviators to
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.60,0:11:43.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,以固定翼飞机做不到的方式飞行
Dialogue: 1,0:11:41.60,0:11:43.60,Original,,0,0,0,,fly in ways that aeroplanes cannot.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.56,0:11:47.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,这架直升机用达索CATIA三维软件设计
Dialogue: 1,0:11:44.56,0:11:47.92,Original,,0,0,0,,This helicopter is created with a CATIA 3D program,
Dialogue: 2,0:11:44.56,0:11:48.06,Annotation,,0,0,0,,CATIA：达索三维设计软件
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.48,0:11:50.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,一种辅助设计的计算机软件
Dialogue: 1,0:11:48.48,0:11:50.24,Original,,0,0,0,,design-assisting computer software.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.20,0:11:53.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,从绘图阶段到样机装配
Dialogue: 1,0:11:51.20,0:11:53.52,Original,,0,0,0,,It takes 700 hours of work between the
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.60,0:11:56.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,需要耗时700个小时
Dialogue: 1,0:11:53.60,0:11:56.00,Original,,0,0,0,,drawing stage and assembly of the pattern.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.00,0:12:01.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,直升机由碳纤维制成
Dialogue: 1,0:12:00.00,0:12:01.84,Original,,0,0,0,,The helicopter is made of carbon fibre,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.84,0:12:04.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,一种比钢更轻更强的复合材料
Dialogue: 1,0:12:01.84,0:12:04.96,Original,,0,0,0,,a composite material lighter and stronger than steel.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.76,0:12:08.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,碳纤维由超声波控制的刀片裁切
Dialogue: 1,0:12:05.76,0:12:08.88,Original,,0,0,0,,The fibre is cut with a blade controlled by ultrasound.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.80,0:12:14.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,多层纤维叠加，构成后机身
Dialogue: 1,0:12:10.80,0:12:14.48,Original,,0,0,0,,Several thicknesses of fibre are added to make the rear fuselage.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.36,0:12:18.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,激光的绿光辅助定位各个部件
Dialogue: 1,0:12:15.36,0:12:18.40,Original,,0,0,0,,The green light of a laser helps position the parts.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.04,0:12:21.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,接着用热风枪贴敷蜂窝网层
Dialogue: 1,0:12:19.04,0:12:21.84,Original,,0,0,0,,Then, with a heat gun, honeycomb mesh is applied,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.16,0:12:24.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,以增强结构的坚固性
Dialogue: 1,0:12:22.16,0:12:24.40,Original,,0,0,0,,which increases the solidity of the structure.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.20,0:12:31.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,但此时碳纤维仍然柔软
Dialogue: 1,0:12:29.20,0:12:31.12,Original,,0,0,0,,But the carbon fibre is still soft.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.00,0:12:35.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,要使其硬化，需在此热压罐中加压烘烤10小时
Dialogue: 1,0:12:32.00,0:12:35.76,Original,,0,0,0,,To harden, it must be baked under pressure for 10 hours in this
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.84,0:12:39.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,温度177℃
Dialogue: 1,0:12:35.84,0:12:39.44,Original,,0,0,0,,autoclave oven at 177 degrees centigrade.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.08,0:12:44.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,工件出炉，进入机加工工序
Dialogue: 1,0:12:42.08,0:12:44.48,Original,,0,0,0,,The pieces exit the oven and head for machining.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.44,0:12:49.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,发动机舱的舱门被夹在切割夹具中手工修形
Dialogue: 1,0:12:45.44,0:12:49.60,Original,,0,0,0,,The door for the motor housing is clamped in a cutting jig and is shaped manually.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.96,0:12:55.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,安装前，用共振锤敲击部件以检测缺陷
Dialogue: 1,0:12:50.96,0:12:55.76,Original,,0,0,0,,Before installing the part, it's struck with a resonance hammer to detect any faults.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.40,0:13:03.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,接着，线束在装配板上铺设成型
Dialogue: 1,0:13:00.40,0:13:03.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Next, the electrical harness is mounted on a pattern board
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.68,0:13:05.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,然后装进飞机
Dialogue: 1,0:13:03.68,0:13:05.44,Original,,0,0,0,,before being installed in the aircraft.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.40,0:13:09.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,这架直升机有超过2公里的线缆
Dialogue: 1,0:13:06.40,0:13:09.20,Original,,0,0,0,,This helicopter has over 2 kilometres of wiring.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.76,0:13:11.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,其他机型可长达近9公里
Dialogue: 1,0:13:09.76,0:13:11.68,Original,,0,0,0,,Others can have almost nine.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.48,0:13:15.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,线缆将连接至飞行仪表
Dialogue: 1,0:13:12.48,0:13:15.12,Original,,0,0,0,,The wiring will be connected to the flight instruments
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.12,0:13:17.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,面板，也就是直升机的大脑
Dialogue: 1,0:13:15.12,0:13:17.04,Original,,0,0,0,,panel, the brain of the helicopter.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.16,0:13:23.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,这架飞机有9964颗铆钉，用铆钉枪紧固
Dialogue: 1,0:13:18.16,0:13:23.04,Original,,0,0,0,,This aircraft has 9,964 rivets fastened with a gun.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.88,0:13:27.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,接下来组装直升机的后机身
Dialogue: 1,0:13:24.88,0:13:27.92,Original,,0,0,0,,The helicopter's rear fuselage is assembled next.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.36,0:13:40.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,飞机的主体结构逐渐成形
Dialogue: 1,0:13:37.36,0:13:40.64,Original,,0,0,0,,Piece by piece, the superstructure of the aircraft takes shape.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.76,0:13:55.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,重达120公斤的发动机即将登场
Dialogue: 1,0:13:51.76,0:13:55.04,Original,,0,0,0,,120 kilos of motor is next in line.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.92,0:14:05.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,正在检查至关重要的旋翼桨叶的安装基座
Dialogue: 1,0:14:00.92,0:14:05.60,Original,,0,0,0,,The all-important circular plate on which the blades will be attached is checked.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.16,0:14:07.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,安全第一
Dialogue: 1,0:14:06.16,0:14:07.36,Original,,0,0,0,,Safety is primary.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.32,0:14:10.16,Translation,,0,0,0,,钻出螺帽孔
Dialogue: 1,0:14:08.32,0:14:10.16,Original,,0,0,0,,The screw nut holes are perforated,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.40,0:14:12.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,以便穿入刹车钢索
Dialogue: 1,0:14:10.40,0:14:12.64,Original,,0,0,0,,allowing the insertion of the brake cable.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.08,0:14:16.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,紧编的金属丝防止螺帽
Dialogue: 1,0:14:14.08,0:14:16.80,Original,,0,0,0,,The tightly braided metal wire prevents the nut from
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.80,0:14:18.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,因剧烈震动而松动
Dialogue: 1,0:14:16.80,0:14:18.72,Original,,0,0,0,,loosening due to strong vibrations.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.64,0:14:28.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,四片产生升力、让直升机飞起来的旋翼桨叶
Dialogue: 1,0:14:24.64,0:14:28.64,Original,,0,0,0,,The four rotor blades, which create the lift and makes the helicopter fly,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.64,0:14:30.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,被逐一卡入安装位
Dialogue: 1,0:14:28.64,0:14:30.24,Original,,0,0,0,,are slotted into place.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.88,0:14:34.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,仪表板装入驾驶舱
Dialogue: 1,0:14:32.88,0:14:34.88,Original,,0,0,0,,The dashboard is installed in the cockpit,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.88,0:14:38.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,并接通各处线缆，完成连接
Dialogue: 1,0:14:34.88,0:14:38.24,Original,,0,0,0,,and the wires are hooked up where contact is established.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.10,0:14:53.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,机舱内部开始装修
Dialogue: 1,0:14:51.10,0:14:53.28,Original,,0,0,0,,The interior of the craft is created.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.16,0:14:57.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,座椅、安全带、控制台、隔板
Dialogue: 1,0:14:54.16,0:14:57.28,Original,,0,0,0,,Seats, safety belts, consoles, bulkheads,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.36,0:15:00.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,舷窗、舱门以及内饰装潢一一安装到位
Dialogue: 1,0:14:57.36,0:15:00.48,Original,,0,0,0,,windows and doors, as well as the trimmings, are installed.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.08,0:15:17.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,直升机已近乎完工，只待喷漆
Dialogue: 1,0:15:13.08,0:15:17.04,Original,,0,0,0,,The helicopter is almost completed, and just awaits a paint job.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.20,0:15:19.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,喷漆完成后
Dialogue: 1,0:15:19.20,0:15:19.76,Original,,0,0,0,,When done.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.24,0:15:22.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,直升机被牵引到外部的总装机库
Dialogue: 1,0:15:20.24,0:15:22.88,Original,,0,0,0,,The helicopter is towed outside to the assembly hangar.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.00,0:15:26.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,进行飞行测试，确保
Dialogue: 1,0:15:24.00,0:15:26.24,Original,,0,0,0,,Flight tests are performed to make sure that
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.24,0:15:29.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,机械与电气部件运转正常
Dialogue: 1,0:15:26.24,0:15:29.68,Original,,0,0,0,,mechanical and electrical components are functioning properly.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.84,0:15:44.72,Translation,,0,0,0,,组装这架直升机，耗时110天，3419个零件，
Dialogue: 1,0:15:37.84,0:15:44.72,Original,,0,0,0,,It requires an average of 110 days to assemble the 3,419 parts of this helicopter.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.44,0:15:57.14,Translation,,0,0,0,,这种2.8吨的飞行器最高时速可达140节，
Dialogue: 1,0:15:51.44,0:15:57.14,Original,,0,0,0,,These 2.8 ton machines are capable of reaching speeds of 140 knots, 
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.14,0:16:02.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,最大飞行高度6096米
Dialogue: 1,0:15:57.14,0:16:02.08,Original,,0,0,0,,and flying at a maximum altitude of 6,096 meters.
Dialogue: 2,0:15:51.44,0:15:57.14,Annotation,,0,0,0,,140节≈259公里/时
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.04,0:16:16.88,Translation,,0,0,0,,啤酒的历史和文明一样悠久
Dialogue: 1,0:16:13.04,0:16:16.88,Original,,0,0,0,,Beer has been around for as long as civilisation itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.68,0:16:20.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,史料记载，古人类用大麦、啤酒花、
Dialogue: 1,0:16:17.68,0:16:20.96,Original,,0,0,0,,Historical records show that ancient peoples made beer
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.96,0:16:23.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,水和酵母酿造啤酒
Dialogue: 1,0:16:20.96,0:16:23.44,Original,,0,0,0,,with barley, hops, water and yeast.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.64,0:16:27.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,今天，我们仍在使用同样的原料
Dialogue: 1,0:16:24.64,0:16:27.12,Original,,0,0,0,,Today we still use the same ingredients,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.44,0:16:29.92,Translation,,0,0,0,,但工艺已今非昔比
Dialogue: 1,0:16:27.44,0:16:29.92,Original,,0,0,0,,but the process has changed dramatically.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.44,0:16:42.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,史料显示，6000年前的美索不达米亚人就开始喝啤酒
Dialogue: 1,0:16:37.44,0:16:42.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Records show that beer was drunk 6,000 years ago in Mesopotamia.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.56,0:16:47.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,苏美尔人用它作神圣的饮品，原料是谷物，但不用啤酒花
Dialogue: 1,0:16:42.56,0:16:47.04,Original,,0,0,0,,The Sumerians made it as a sacred beverage from grains, but without hops.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.76,0:16:51.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,高卢人和凯尔特人喝的是大麦、小麦和米酿造的饮品
Dialogue: 1,0:16:47.76,0:16:51.36,Original,,0,0,0,,The Gauls and the Celts drank a beverage made with barley, wheat and rice.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.56,0:16:56.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,十字军东征期间，欧洲人发现了香料，用
Dialogue: 1,0:16:52.56,0:16:56.56,Original,,0,0,0,,During the Crusades, Europeans discovered spices and flavoured the
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.56,0:16:58.32,Translation,,0,0,0,,肉桂和月桂叶给饮品调味
Dialogue: 1,0:16:56.56,0:16:58.32,Original,,0,0,0,,beverage with cinnamon and laurel.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.28,0:17:02.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,15世纪，啤酒花作为一种香料被引入
Dialogue: 1,0:16:59.28,0:17:02.40,Original,,0,0,0,,In the 15th century, hops were introduced as a spice,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.88,0:17:05.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,这才诞生了我们今天所熟知的啤酒
Dialogue: 1,0:17:02.88,0:17:05.04,Original,,0,0,0,,giving rise to the beer we know today.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.24,0:17:16.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,欢迎来到许多人的梦想之地——啤酒厂
Dialogue: 1,0:17:12.24,0:17:16.80,Original,,0,0,0,,Welcome to the fantasy of many, a brewery, a beer factory.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.52,0:17:20.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,简单说，啤酒是一种发酵饮品
Dialogue: 1,0:17:17.52,0:17:20.00,Original,,0,0,0,,Put simply, beer is a fermented beverage.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.08,0:17:21.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,由谷物和水酿制而成
Dialogue: 1,0:17:20.08,0:17:21.76,Original,,0,0,0,,Made with cereals and water.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.36,0:17:25.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,首先到场的是麦芽大麦
Dialogue: 1,0:17:23.36,0:17:25.60,Original,,0,0,0,,First to arrive is the malted barley.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.72,0:17:29.60,Translation,,0,0,0,,这家工厂拥有自己的水过滤系统
Dialogue: 1,0:17:26.72,0:17:29.60,Original,,0,0,0,,This facility has its own water filtration plant.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.08,0:17:33.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,使用前会再次过滤，去除氯
Dialogue: 1,0:17:30.08,0:17:33.52,Original,,0,0,0,,It will be refiltered before being used to eliminate chlorine.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.64,0:17:37.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,这个储罐可容纳8万升水
Dialogue: 1,0:17:34.64,0:17:37.28,Original,,0,0,0,,This tank can hold 80,000 litres of water.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.12,0:17:42.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,加入10至15吨麦芽和谷物
Dialogue: 1,0:17:39.12,0:17:42.64,Original,,0,0,0,,Between 10 to 15 tons of malt and grain are added.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.36,0:17:47.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,这款啤酒偏爱经过热处理的深色麦芽
Dialogue: 1,0:17:43.36,0:17:47.84,Original,,0,0,0,,In this beer, dark malt, which has been heat treated, is the preferred variety.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.08,0:17:55.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,搅拌器防止麦壳沉到罐底
Dialogue: 1,0:17:52.08,0:17:55.68,Original,,0,0,0,,Agitators prevent malt husks from settling at the bottom of the tank.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.80,0:18:02.64,Translation,,0,0,0,,原料在罐中浸泡2小时，变成一种叫"麦芽汁"的甜味液体
Dialogue: 1,0:17:56.80,0:18:02.64,Original,,0,0,0,,The preparation spends 2 hours in the tank, where it becomes a sweet-tasting liquid called wort.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.08,0:18:12.08,Translation,,0,0,0,,麦芽汁将被提取出来，然后煮沸
Dialogue: 1,0:18:09.08,0:18:12.08,Original,,0,0,0,,The wort will be extracted and then boiled.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.30,0:18:19.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,抽取样本进行检测
Dialogue: 1,0:18:17.30,0:18:19.44,Original,,0,0,0,,A sample is drawn off for testing.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.16,0:18:24.80,Translation,,0,0,0,,这是酿酒各阶段众多受控检测中的第一项
Dialogue: 1,0:18:20.16,0:18:24.80,Original,,0,0,0,,This is the first of many controlled tests carried out at various stages of brewing.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.00,0:18:33.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,这就是酒糟，从麦芽汁中滤出的固体残渣
Dialogue: 1,0:18:30.00,0:18:33.52,Original,,0,0,0,,This is the draff, a solid residue extracted from the wort.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.40,0:18:36.00,Translation,,0,0,0,,它将被用作牲畜饲料
Dialogue: 1,0:18:34.40,0:18:36.00,Original,,0,0,0,,It will be used as cattle feed.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.30,0:18:48.24,Translation,,0,0,0,,接着过滤液体，将麦芽汁与麦壳分离
Dialogue: 1,0:18:44.30,0:18:48.24,Original,,0,0,0,,The liquid is then filtered, where the wort is separated from the malt husks.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.56,0:18:53.36,Translation,,0,0,0,,从麦芽汁加热器中取样，以检验
Dialogue: 1,0:18:50.56,0:18:53.36,Original,,0,0,0,,A sample is taken from the wort heater to verify the
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.44,0:18:59.04,Translation,,0,0,0,,糖的密度和麦芽汁的品质
Dialogue: 1,0:18:53.44,0:18:59.04,Original,,0,0,0,,density of sugars and the quality of the wort.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.80,0:19:11.12,Translation,,0,0,0,,现在，向麦芽汁加热器中加入啤酒花
Dialogue: 1,0:19:08.80,0:19:11.12,Original,,0,0,0,,Now the hops are added into the wort heater.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.84,0:19:14.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,啤酒花赋予啤酒苦味与香气
Dialogue: 1,0:19:11.84,0:19:14.48,Original,,0,0,0,,The hops impart the bitterness and aroma of the beer.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.80,0:19:18.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,啤酒花以颗粒形态加入
Dialogue: 1,0:19:16.80,0:19:18.56,Original,,0,0,0,,The hops come in pellet form.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.24,0:19:27.68,Translation,,0,0,0,,在控制室里，操作员掌控着酿造流程
Dialogue: 1,0:19:24.24,0:19:27.68,Original,,0,0,0,,In the control room, an operator handles the brewing process.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.00,0:19:37.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,加入启动发酵的酵母
Dialogue: 1,0:19:34.00,0:19:37.20,Original,,0,0,0,,The yeast, which starts off the fermentation, is added.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.60,0:19:40.56,Translation,,0,0,0,,这一过程持续7至10天
Dialogue: 1,0:19:37.60,0:19:40.56,Original,,0,0,0,,A process that lasts between 7 and 10 days.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.12,0:19:45.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,泡沫的出现表明发酵已经开始
Dialogue: 1,0:19:41.12,0:19:45.44,Original,,0,0,0,,The presence of foam indicates that fermentation has begun.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.12,0:19:49.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,每个发酵罐都由电脑控制
Dialogue: 1,0:19:47.12,0:19:49.76,Original,,0,0,0,,Each fermentation tank is computer controlled to
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.76,0:19:51.52,Translation,,0,0,0,,以维持特定温度
Dialogue: 1,0:19:49.76,0:19:51.52,Original,,0,0,0,,maintain a specific temperature.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.32,0:19:55.10,Translation,,0,0,0,,化学反应产生漂浮的浮沫
Dialogue: 1,0:19:52.32,0:19:55.10,Original,,0,0,0,,Chemical reactions create the floating scum.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.60,0:20:03.44,Translation,,0,0,0,,陈酿三周后，啤酒已接近成品
Dialogue: 1,0:20:00.00,0:20:03.44,Original,,0,0,0,,Now aged for 3 weeks, the beer is almost finished.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.08,0:20:06.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,这些巨大的容器是灌装罐
Dialogue: 1,0:20:04.08,0:20:06.40,Original,,0,0,0,,These huge containers are the bottling tanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.84,0:20:13.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,啤酒还需再过滤一次
Dialogue: 1,0:20:11.84,0:20:13.76,Original,,0,0,0,,The beer has to be filtered once more.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.72,0:20:19.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,啤酒被澄清，去除导致啤酒浑浊的成分
Dialogue: 1,0:20:14.72,0:20:19.76,Original,,0,0,0,,The water is clarified, then rid of the components responsible for the cloudiness of the beer.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.20,0:20:23.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,这是经过第二次过滤的啤酒
Dialogue: 1,0:20:21.20,0:20:23.20,Original,,0,0,0,,Here's the beer filtered a second time,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.68,0:20:26.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,最终成为清亮透明的成品
Dialogue: 1,0:20:23.68,0:20:26.40,Original,,0,0,0,,and finally finished as a clear product.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.40,0:20:31.28,Translation,,0,0,0,,回收的瓶子被清洗并消毒
Dialogue: 1,0:20:28.40,0:20:31.28,Original,,0,0,0,,Used bottles are washed, where they become sterilized.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.08,0:20:43.20,Translation,,0,0,0,,移动平台将空瓶送到灌装位
Dialogue: 1,0:20:40.08,0:20:43.20,Original,,0,0,0,,A moving plate transports the empty bottles into place.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.80,0:20:50.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,灌装机一边移动，一边每分钟灌装约1000瓶
Dialogue: 1,0:20:46.80,0:20:50.40,Original,,0,0,0,,About a thousand bottles a minute are filled while on the move.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.34,0:21:02.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,随后进入封盖机，再送往巴氏杀菌单元
Dialogue: 1,0:20:58.34,0:21:02.76,Original,,0,0,0,,Then onto the capper before being sent to the pasteurization unit.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.18,0:21:19.76,Translation,,0,0,0,,最后两步是贴标和包装
Dialogue: 1,0:21:16.18,0:21:19.76,Original,,0,0,0,,The final two steps are labelling and packaging.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.80,0:21:28.96,Translation,,0,0,0,,由水和谷物酿成
Dialogue: 1,0:21:26.80,0:21:28.96,Original,,0,0,0,,Made from water and cereal grains,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.28,0:21:32.40,Translation,,0,0,0,,啤酒现在可以开怀畅饮了
Dialogue: 1,0:21:29.28,0:21:32.40,Original,,0,0,0,,the beer is now ready to be consumed and enjoyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.12,0:21:38.48,Translation,,0,0,0,,整个酿造过程约需4周，而喝掉它只需30秒
Dialogue: 1,0:21:33.12,0:21:38.48,Original,,0,0,0,,The whole process lasts around 4 weeks and takes about 30 seconds to drink.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.52,0:21:39.84,Translation,,0,0,0,,干杯
Dialogue: 1,0:21:39.52,0:21:39.84,Original,,0,0,0,,Cheers.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.84,0:21:42.84,Original,,0,0,0,,
